$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General Procedure D: A red cap sealed tube (25-30 ml in volume) equipped
with a stirring bar was heated and cooled under vacuum and back-filled
with argon. [Cp*RhCl2]2 (15.5 mg, 0.025 mmol, 5 mol%) and CsOAc (191 mg,
1.0 mmol, 2.0 eq.) were weighed into the reaction vessel in glovebox.
Npivaloyloxybenzamide substrate (1) (0.5 mmol, 1.0 eq.), PivOH (24 mg,
0.25 mmol, 0.5 eq.) and dry MeOH (2.5 mL) was added under a stream of
argon. N-Chloroamine substrate 2 (1.0 mmol, 2.0 eq.) was added to the
solution and the reaction was allowed to stir at room temperature for 16
h. As monitored by TLC analysis, in case of incomplete conversion,
N-Chloroamine and CsOAc (both 1.0 eq. each time) were added stepwise
until TLC analysis indicated maximum conversion. The reaction mixture was
then diluted with EtOAc (2 mL) and filtered through a short pad of
silica. The silica pad was washed with EtOAc (3 x 4 mL). The combined
filtrates were concentrated under reduced pressure using a rotary
evaporator (40-45 °C). 2-Morpholino-N-(pivaloyloxy)benzamide (3ba) as a
colorless oil, yield 245 mg, 0.80 mmol, 80%. RF (pentane/EtOAc 85:15):
0.22; 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3) δ = 13.49 (s, 1H, NH), 8.21-8.08 (m, 1H,
CHar), 7.51 (ddd, J = 8.1, 7.2, 1.8 Hz, 1H, CHar), 7.36-7.28 (m, 2H,
CHar), 3.96 -3.87 (m, 4H, CH2), 3.07-2.99 (m, 4H, CH2), 1.36 (s, 9H,
C(CH3)3). 13C NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3) δ = 176.3 (CO), 164.2 (CO), 150.7 (Cq),
133.2 (CHar), 131.7 (CHar), 126.9 (Cq), 126.5 (CHar), 122.0 (CHar), 67.1
(CH2), 53.9 (CH2), 38.6 (CMe3), 27.2 (CH3). ESI-MS: calculated
[C16H22N2O4Na]+: 329.1472, found: 329.1466.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective, in case of incomplete conversion, N-chloroamine and CsOAc
(both 1.0 eq. each time) were added stepwise until TLC analysis indicated
maximum conversion, optimization study (optimized on base and catalyst
amount), sealed tube used
