$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: IV-2. General Procedures for the Ru-Catalyzed
Selective C-N Amidation Reaction with Acyl Azides (Scheme 3) To an
oven-dried screw capped vial equipped with a spinvane triangular-shaped
Teflon stirbar were added 2-arylpyiridne (1, 0.2 mmol), acyl azide (2,
0.36 mmol), [RuCl2(p-cymene)]2 (6.1 mg, 5 mol %), AgSbF6 (13.8 mg, 20 mol
%), 2-nitrobenzoic acid (10.0 mg, 30 mol %) and 1,2-dichloroethane (0.5
mL) under atmospheric conditions. The reaction mixture was stirred in a
pre-heated oil bath at 50 °C for 18 h. The reaction was cooled to room
temperature, filtered through a pad of celite and then washed with CH2Cl2
(10 mL x 3). The solvents were removed under reduced pressure and the
crude reaction mixture was purified by silica gel column chromatography
with n-hexane/EtOAc as an eluent. The desired C-N bond forming products
4. N-[5-Methyl-2-(pyridin-2-yl)phenyl]benzamide (Scheme 3, 4b)
N-[5-Methoxy-2-(pyridin-2-yl)phenyl]benzamide (4c) White solid. m.p.
135-136 °C; 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 13.81 (s, 1H), 8.63 - 8.53 (m, 2H),
8.06 (dd, J = 8.0, 1.7 Hz, 2H), 7.82 - 7.68 (m, 2H), 7.67 (d, J = 8.8 Hz,
1H), 7.57 - 7.44 (m, 3H), 7.20 (ddd, J = 7.3, 4.9, 1.3 Hz, 1H), 6.74 (dd,
J = 8.8, 2.7 Hz, 1H), 3.92 (s, 3H); 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ 165.8,
161.1, 158.2, 147.0, 140.1, 137.7, 135.8, 131.5, 129.6, 128.6, 127.4,
122.0, 121.1, 117.6, 110.7, 105.6, 55.5; IR (cm-1) 2920, 2838, 1657,
1582, 1536, 1417, 1247, 1163, 1048, 781; HRMS (EI+) m/z calcd. for
C19H16N2O2 [M]+: 304.1212, found: 304.1213.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM chemoselective, product depends on catalyst used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Orthogonal Reactivity of Acyl Azides in C-H Activation: Dichotomy between
C-C and C-N Amidations Based on Catalyst Systems
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Shin, Kwangmin; Ryu, Jaeyune; Chang, Sukbok
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2014), 16(7), 2022-2025

