$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: 6. One-pot Direct Amination using NCS5 To an
amber 8 mL-vial (vial A), [Cp*RhCl2]2 (2.5 mol %, 3.1 mg), CsOAc (30 mol
%, 11.5 mg) and AgSbF6 (1.5 equiv, 103 mg) were added, and the vial was
sealed with a Teflon® liner cap. To another amber 4-mL vial,
N-chlorosuccinimide (1.2 equiv, 32.4 mg) was added and was also sealed
with a Teflon® liner cap (vial B). Both vials were evacuated and back
filled with N2 for three times. Freshly distilled THF (0.5 mL) and amine
(1.1 equiv) were added to the vial B, and the mixture was stirred at room
temperature for 20 min. Freshly distilled THF (0.5 mL) was then added to
the vial A, followed by the addition of oxime (0.2 mmol) with a 50-μL
syringe. The mixture in vial A was preheated at 40 °C for 5 min. The
mixture in vial B was transferred to vial A with an 1-mL syringe in one
portion. The reaction mixture was allowed to stir at 40 °C for 1 h. After
cooling to room temperature, 30% aqueous ammonia (2 mL) and EtOAc (5 mL)
were added. The organic layer was collected, and the aqueous layer was
washed with EtOAc (5 mL x 2). The combined organic fractions were dried
over Na2SO4 and then filtered through a short plug of Celite®. Solvents
were removed by rotary evaporation, and the residue was re-dissolved in a
small amount of dichloromethane (DCM) for flash column chromatography.
3ab, yield 79%. Rf = 0.55 (10% EtOAc in hexanes); 1H NMR (CDCl3, 400
MHz): δH 7.32- 7.27 (m, 2H), 7.04-6.97 (m, 2H), 3.98 (s, 3H), 2.93 (bt, J
= 5.2 Hz, 4H), 2.25 (s, 3H), 1.70-1.65 (m, 4H), 1.56-1.52 (m, 2H); 13C
NMR (CDCl3, 100 MHz) δC 159.11 (C), 152.06 (C), 131.95 (C), 130.05 (CH),
129.54 (CH), 122.19 (CH), 118.81 (CH), 61.55 (CH3), 53.29 (CH2), 26.40
(CH2), 24.22 (CH2), 14.86 (CH3); IR (neat, cm-1): 2935, 1487, 1447, 1448,
1381, 1228, 1053, 1042, 881; HRMS m/z (ESI): calculated for C14H21N2O+:
233.1654, found: 233.1646.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective, alternative preparation shown, amber vial used, the
mixture from the first stage and the mixture from the second stage were
mixed the third stage, sealed tube used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Rhodium(III)-Catalyzed Intermolecular Direct Amination of Aromatic C-H
Bonds with N-Chloroamines
