$DATUM IV-2. General Procedures for the Ru-Catalyzed Selective C-N Amidation
Reaction with Acyl Azides (Scheme 3) To an oven-dried screw capped vial
equipped with a spinvane triangular-shaped Teflon stirbar were added
2-arylpyiridne (1, 0.2 mmol), acyl azide (2, 0.36 mmol),
[RuCl2(p-cymene)]2 (6.1 mg, 5 mol %), AgSbF6 (13.8 mg, 20 mol %),
2-nitrobenzoic acid (10.0 mg, 30 mol %) and 1,2-dichloroethane (0.5 mL)
under atmospheric conditions. The reaction mixture was stirred in a
pre-heated oil bath at 50 °C for 18 h. The reaction was cooled to room
temperature, filtered through a pad of celite and then washed with CH2Cl2
(10 mL x 3). The solvents were removed under reduced pressure and the
crude reaction mixture was purified by silica gel column chromatography
with n-hexane/EtOAc as an eluent. The desired C-N bond forming products
4. N-[5-Methyl-2-(pyridin-2-yl)phenyl]benzamide (Scheme 3, 4b) White
solid. m.p. 100-101 °C; 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 13.42 (s, 1H), 8.67
(dd, J = 1.7, 0.9 Hz, 1H), 8.62 (ddd, J = 4.9, 1.8, 1.0 Hz, 1H), 8.04
(dd, J = 7.8, 1.8 Hz, 2H), 7.83 - 7.71 (m, 2H), 7.61 (d, J = 8.0 Hz, 1H),
7.55 - 7.44 (m, 3H), 7.22 (ddd, J = 7.1, 4.9, 1.5 Hz, 1H), 6.99 (ddd, J =
7.9, 1.8, 0.8 Hz, 1H), 2.44 (s, 3H); 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ 165.5,
158.4, 147.1, 140.7, 138.1, 137.7, 135.9, 131.5, 128.6, 128.6, 127.4,
124.4, 122.7, 122.6, 122.2, 121.6, 21.7; IR (cm-1) 2916, 2853, 1665,
1579, 1534, 1469, 1414, 1281, 785, 680; HRMS (EI+) m/z calcd. for
C19H16N2O [M]+: 288.1263, found: 288.1260.
