$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Typical Procedure for the Preparation of
2-Aminobenzimidazoles 3a-p by the Reaction of Arylguanidine and
Phenyliodine(III) Bis(trifloroacetate): In a 25 mL of flask,
phenyliodine(III) bis(trifloroacetate) (0.33 mmol, 146 mg) was added to
an arylguanidine (0.30 mmol) in MeCN (5 mL), and the mixture was stirred
at 80 °C temperature for 4 h. The solvent of the reaction mixture was
evaporated under vacuum. The residue was purified by chromatography with
PE and ethyl acetate to give products. Compound 3j. Yield: 71% (0.3 mmol,
74 mg), yellow solid. mp: 54.6-55.8 °C; 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ
1.26-1.29 (m, 2H, CH2), 1.45-1.67 (m, 8H, CH2), 2.04-2.10 (m, 2H, CH2),
2.34 (s, 3H, CH3), 2.47 (s, 3H, CH3), 4.03 (d, J = 8.3 Hz, 1H, NH)
4.08-4.17 (m, 1H, CH), 6.70 (s, 1H, CH), 6.92 (d, J = 8.0 Hz, 1H, CH),
7.26-7.29 (m, 2H, CH), 7.37-7.39 (m, 3H, CH); 13C NMR (125 MHz, CDCl3): δ
21.21, 21.45, 23.75, 28.16, 25.47, 53.73, 108.15, 115.76, 122.50, 126.89,
129.28, 130.99, 132.32, 135.47, 138.70, 140.58, 152.77. HRMS calcd. for
C22H28N3 [M+H]+ : 334.2283, found 334.2287.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
