$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 2-Amino-3-methoxynaphthalene (2ad).46 To an oven-dried 25 mL round-bottom
flask, cooled to room temperature under Ar atmosphere, were added
2-methoxynaphthalene (158 mg, 1.0 mmol) and THF (5 mL). The mixture was
cooled to 0°C, and to it was added n-BuLi (1.2 equiv, 0.75 mL), dropwise
via syringe as a 1.6 M solution in hexanes. The mixture was stirred for 1
h at 0°C, and then to it was added B(OiPr)3 (1.5 equiv, 0.35 mL). The
ice-water bath was removed and the mixture allowed to warm to room
temperature. A freshly prepared solution of HSA (1.5 equiv, 170 mg) in 1
M aqueous NaOH (5 mL) was added and the resulting biphasic mixture
stirred for 16 h at room temperature. The reaction mixture was diluted
with H2O and extracted with EtOAc (2 × 30 mL). The combined organic
extracts were dried (Na2SO4) and concentrated in vacuo. The residue was
purified by flash chromatography (EtOAc/hexanes). The amine product (2ad:
133 mg, 77%), which had 1H and 13C NMR data that matched with that
reported in the literature.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM green chemistry, dropwise addition of nBuLi/Hexane (stage 1)
