$DATUM Synthesis of 4-amino dibenzo 18-crown-6 ether (3) [30] In 100 ml round
bottom flask Polyphosphoric acid (10-20 gm), dibenzo 18-crown-6 (10 mmol)
and sodium azide (11 mmol) were charged. Then the reaction mixture was
heated at 100°C for 3 hr. After completion of reaction (monitored by
TLC), mixture was poured in to 500 ml water under vigorous stirring.
Adjust the pH 8-9 by ammonium hydroxide and the precipitate formed was
filtered off. The reaction product in to mother liquor extracted with 3
times 200 ml methylene dichloride. Then all the methylene dichloride was
combined and dried by Na2SO4. The dried methylene dichloride was
evaporated under rotary evaporator to obtain crude 4-amino dibenzo 18
crown-6 ether residue. Finally, the crude product was recrystallized from
n-butanol, Pure 4-amino dibenzo 18 crown-6 ether (Yield. 62%). 4-amino
dibenzo 18-crown-6 ether (3) White solid; Yield 77%. M.p. 157-160 °C
(Lit.158-163°C). M.p.160-164°C; IR: 3318, 3216, 2975, 2878, 1594, 1508,
1452, 1257, 1225, 1121, 1036, 923 cm-1; 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3): δ 3.48
(brs, 2H, NH2), 4.00-4.05 (m, 7H, OCH2), 4.10-4.15 (m, 4H, OCH2),
4.17-4.21 (m, 5H, OCH2), 6.21-6.24 (m, 1H, Ar-H), 6.30-6.31 (d, 1H,
Ar-H), 6.73-6.75 (d, 1H, Ar-H), 6.90 (s, 4H, Ar-H); Anal. Calcd. for
C20H25NO6 (375.415): C, 63.99; H, 6.71; N, 3.73. Found: C, 63.94; H,
6.67; N, 3.77.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
