$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for the synthesis of
N-substituted indole-3-carbonitrile derivatives usingCH2Cl2 as solvent To
a solution of the substrate 1 (4 mmol) in CH2Cl2 (30 mL) was added
dropwise a solution of PIFA (4.2 mmol) in CH2Cl2 (20 mL) within 30 min
with stirring at room temperature. TLC was used to monitor the reaction
process until the total consumption of 1. To the solution was then added
saturated aq. NaHCO3 solution (10 mL), and the reaction mixture was
stirred further for 5 min. The organic layer was dried with anhydrous
Na2SO4. The solvent was removed under vacuum and the residue was purified
by silica gel chromatography, using a mixture of PE and EA as eluent, to
give the desired products. 2-Methyl-1-phenyl-1H-indole-3-carboxylic acid
ethyl ester (3r) Following the general procedure, 3r was obtained after
silica gel chromatography (8% EA/PE). Yield: 75%, colorless crystal. Rf =
0.43 (EA/PE = 10/90). m.p. 89-90 °C; 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ 8.18 (d,
J = 8.0 Hz, 1H, Harom), 7.58-7.51 (m, 3H, Harom), 7.32-7.12 (m 4H,
Harom), 7.01 (d, J = 8.0 Hz, 1H, Harom), 4.43 (q, J = 7.2 Hz, °CH2), 2.59
(s, 3H, CH3), 1.47 (t, J = 7.2 Hz, CH3). 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3): δ
166.2 (C), 145.5 (C), 137.8 (C), 136.7 (C), 129.8 (CH), 128.9 (CH), 128.3
(CH), 126.7 (C), 122.5 (CH), 122.2 (CH), 121.4 (CH), 110.5 (CH), 105.3
(C), 59.6 (°CH2), 14.8 (CH3), 13.1 (CH3). HRMS (ESI) m/z calcd for
C18H18NO2 [M+H+] 280.1332, found 280.1338.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis of N-substituted indole derivatives via PIFA-mediated
intramolecular cyclization
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Du, Yunfei; Liu, Renhe; Linn, Gregory; Zhao, Kang
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2006), 8(26), 5919-5922

