$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for the preparation of
polyheterocycles (9a-b, 14a-h and 17a-b) A solution of 6-azido-2-pyridone
(0.36 mmol) in 1,2-dichloroethane (3.5 mL) in a sealed vial was heated
under microwave irradiations at 120 °C for 5 minutes. After completion of
reaction solvent was removed under reduced pressure. The crude product
was purified with silica gel chromatography by eluting with
(Dichloromethane:Ethyl acetate 7:3→4:6). Final products were lyophilized
from acetonitrile:water (1:3) mixture. Methyl
(12R)-10-oxo-16-[m-(trifluoromethyl)phenyl]-14-thia-8.11-diazatetracyclo[7.7.0.02,7.011,15]hexadeca-1(9),2,4,6,15-pentaene-12-carboxylate(9b):
Prepared by following the general procedure, 51 mg of 8b was converted to
36 mg (75%) of 9b isolated as white solid. [α]D-26 (c 1.2, DMSO); IR ν
1750, 1670, 1581, 1435, 1238 cm-1; 1H-NMR (400 MHz, DMSO-d6 ) δ 3.61 (dd,
J = 2.0, 11.6 Hz, 1H), 3.77 (s, 3H), 3.94 (dd, J = 8.4, 11.6 Hz, 1H),
5.81 (d, J = 2.0, 8.4 Hz, 1H), 6.86-6.95 (m, 2H), 7.32-7.36 (m, 1H), 7.54
(d, J = 8.4 Hz, 1H), 7.82-7.89 (m, 4H), 11.98 (s, 1H);13C-NMR (100 MHz,
DMSO-d6 ) δ 31.4, 52.4, 62.3, 108.2, 112.6, 119.3, 120.2, 121.0, 123.3,
124.6, 125.2, 126.0, 129.8, 133.6, 134.6, 136.3, 137.3, 139.7, 153.3,
168.5. HRMS (EI) calcd (M+Na)+ C22H15F3N2NaO3S+ 467.0647 observed
467.0604.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM green chemistry, green chemistry-process simplification, microwave
irradiation, sealed tube used
