$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure of Pd(II)-Catalyzed
Amination of C-H Bonds: In a 20 mL seal tube,
2-pyridinesulfonyl-protected phenethylamine derivatives 1a-1o (0.2 mmol,
1 equiv), Pd(OAc)2 (4.5 mg, 0.1 equiv), PhI(OAc)2 (129 mg, 2 equiv) were
dissolved in 20 mL dry toluene under air. The tube was sealed with a
Teflon lined cap, and the reaction mixture was stirred at 130 °C for 4 h.
After cooled to room temperature, the mixture was concentrated under
vacuum and the residue was purified by column chromatography on silica
gel with a gradient eluent of hexane and ethyl acetate. The corresponding
products. Product: 2b. 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 8.61 (d, J = 4.4 Hz,
1H), 7.96 (d, J = 8.0 Hz, 1H), 7.82 (dt, J 1 = 1.6 Hz, J 2 = 8.0 Hz, 1H),
7.40-7.43 (m, 1H), 7.28 (d, J = 8.0 Hz, 1H), 7.00 (t, J = 8.0 Hz, 1H),
7.75 (d, J = 8.0 Hz, 1H), 4.34 (t, J = 8.4 Hz, 2H), 2.96 (t, J = 8.4 Hz,
2H), 2.15 (s, 3H); 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ 156.1, 150.1, 141.1, 137.7,
134.6, 130.5, 127.5, 126.9, 124.6, 123.0, 111.6, 51.1, 26.8, 18.6; HRMS
(ESI-TOF) calcd. for C14H15N2O2S ([M+H]+): 275.0849, Found: 275.0850.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM sealed tube used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis of Indolines via Pd(II)-Catalyzed Amination of C-H Bonds Using
PhI(OAc)2 as the Bystanding Oxidant
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Mei, Tian-Sheng; Leow, Dasheng; Xiao, Han; Laforteza, Brian N.; Yu,
Jin-Quan
