$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: B. Sodium hydride (60% suspension in oil,
0.120 g, 3.0 mmol) was added to a solution of the aromatic amine (3.0
mmol) in N,N-dimethylaniline (5 ml), and then (after the hydrogen
evolution ceased) 1,3,7-triazapyrene (1) (0.103 g, 0.5 mmol) was added.
The mixture was heated to 80-85°C and stirred at that temperature for the
duration indicated in Table 1. The further isolation was performed
according to the method A. 6-Phenylamino-1,3,7-triazapyrene (2a). Yield:
0.111 g (75%), yellow-orange crystals, time: 8 h. mp 262-263°C (EtOH). 1H
NMR spectrum, δ, ppm (J, Hz): 7.17 (1H, t, J = 7.3, H-4 Ph); 7.46 (2H,
dd, J = 7.3, J = 8.3, H-3,5 Ph); 7.76 (1H, d, J = 9.3, H-4); 7.91 (2H, d,
J = 8.3, H-2,6 Ph); 8.09 (1H, d, J = 9.2, H-10); 8.52 (1H, d, J = 9.2,
H-9); 9.15 (1H, d, J = 9.3, H-5); 9.25 (1H, s, H-8); 9.56 (1H, s, H-2);
10.04 (1H, br. s, NH). 13C NMR spectrum, δ, ppm: 157.6; 155.7; 153.5;
152.7; 149.0; 140.0; 135.4; 130.9; 128.5; 127.6; 124.9; 123.2; 122.5;
121.6; 117.6; 115.8; 109.4. Found, m/z: 297.1141 [M+H]+. C19H13N4.
Calculated, m/z: 297.1135.
