$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General Procedure: In a dry box, aryl halide (2.0 mmol), HBPin (512 mg,
4.0 mmol), (Ind)Ir(COD) (16.6 mg, 0.04 mmol, 2 mol%) and dmpe (6.0 mg,
0.04 mmol, 2 mol%) or dppe (15.9 mg, 0.04 mmol, 2 mol%) were transferred
into a thick-walled air-free flask equipped with a magnetic stirring bar.
The flask was sealed, removed from the glove box, and stirred at 150 °C
(dmpe) or 100 °C (dppe) until the reaction was judged complete by GC-FID.
The reaction mixture was allowed to cool to room temperature and
subsequently placed under vacuum for 1-2 h. The thick walled flask was
brought into the dry box and anhydrous K3PO4 (594 mg, 2.8 mmol, 1.4 eq),
Pd2dba3 (18.3 mg, 0.02 mmol, 1 mol%), P(t-Bu)3 (12.1 mg, 0.06 mmol, 3
mol%) or 2-dicyclohexylphosphino-2’-(N,N-dimethylamino) biphenyl (31.5
mg, 0.08 mmol, 4 mol%) or 2-(dicyclohexylphosphino)biphenyl (28 mg, 0.08
mmol, 4 mol%), amine (2.4-2.6 mmol, 1.2-1.3 eq) and DME (3mL) were added.
The flask was then sealed, removed from the dry box and stirred at 100 °C
until the reaction was judged complete by GC-FID. After completion, the
reaction mixture was extracted three times with ether. The combined
organics were washed with brine followed by water, dried over MgSO4, and
concentrated under reduced pressure. The crude material was then
subjected to column chromatography. Table 2, Entry 1:
N-Phenyl-3-methyl-5-(4,4,5,5-tetramethyl-1,3,2- dioxaboryl)aniline. The
general procedure was applied to 3-chlorotoluene (253.0 mg, 2.0 mmol).
The borylation step was carried out neat with HBPin (512.0 mg, 4.0 mmol)
and dmpe (6.0 mg, 0.04 mmol, 2 mol%) at 150 °C for 8 h. The amination
step was then carried out using P(t-Bu)3 (12.1 mg, 0.06 mmol, 3 mol%) and
aniline (224.0 mg, 2.4 mmol) at 100 °C for 19 h. Column chromatography
(hexanes/CH2Cl2 2:3) furnished the desired product (462.8 mg, 75 %) as a
light yellow oil, which solidified on standing, mp 100 °C. 1H NMR (C6D6,
500 MHz) δ 7.64 (br s, 2 H), 7.07-7.03 (m, 2 H), 6.92-6.89 (m, 2 H), 6.86
(br s, 1 H), 6.77-6.74 (m, 1 H), 5.05 (br s, 1 H), 2.11 (s, 3 H), 1.13
(s, 12 H). 13C NMR (C6D6, 125 MHz) δ 144.0 (C), 143.0 (C), 138.4 (C),
129.5 (CH), 129.2 (CH), 122.5 (CH), 122.2 (CH), 120.7 (CH), 117.8 (CH),
83.7 (C), 24.94 (CH3), 21.34 (CH3). 11B NMR (C6D6, 96 Hz) δ 29.1. FT-IR
(NaCl) 3393, 3365 (sh), 3036, 2979, 2926, 2867, 1590, 1518, 1497, 1470,
1410, 1368, 1312, 1271, 1237, 1215, 1167, 1144, 1117, 1031, 1019, 967,
911, 853, 745, 712, 698, 668 cm-1. LRMS (% rel. int.): m/z 309 (100), 294
(2), 250 (3), 236 (7), 209 (27), 193 (14), 167 (11), 147 (5). Anal. Calcd
for C19H24BO2N: C, 73.80; H, 7.82; N, 4.53. Found: C, 73.82; H, 7.94; N,
4.43.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective, no solvent in stage 1, optimization study
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM One-Pot Borylation/Amination Reactions: Syntheses of Arylamine Boronate
Esters from Halogenated Arenes
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Holmes, Daniel; Chotana, Ghayoor A.; Maleczka, Robert E. Jr.; Smith,
Milton R. III
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2006), 8(7), 1407-1410

