$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: 4-N-Octylamino-benzoic acid. (Table 9, entry
1) 4-Chlorobenzoic acid (0.157 g, 1.00 mmol) was added to a 4 mL vial
containing lithium bis(trimethylsilyl)amide (0.402 g, 2.40 mmol) in 1.0
mL of DME. Pd(OAc)2 and CyPF-t-Bu (50.0 µL from stock solution A, 5.0 x
10-4 mmol) were then added by syringe, followed by octylamine (0.155g,
1.20 mmol). The vial was sealed with a cap containing a PTFE septum, and
the reaction mixture was stirred at 100° C for 20 h. The reaction mixture
then was allowed to cool to room temperature. To the reaction mixture was
added 1 M HCl (0.5-1.0 mL). The mixture was stirred at room temperature
for 5 min and was then extracted with CH2Cl2 (3 x 30.0 mL). The organic
layer was separated and dried over Na2SO4. The solvent was evaporated,
and the crude product was isolated by eluting with hexane/ethyl acetate
(50/50) to give 202.2 mg (81%) of N-octylaminobenzoic acid as a white
solid. 3-N-cyclohexylamino-acetanilide (Table 9, entry 15) The general
procedure C conducted with 3-chloroacetanilide (0.170 g, 1.00 mmol),
cyclohexylamine (0.119g, 1.20 mmol), Pd(OAc)2 and CyPF-t-Bu (50.0 µL from
stock solution A, 5.0 x 10-4 mmol) and lithium bis(trimethylsilyl)amide
(0.402 g, 2.40 mmol) gave 172.6 mg (74%) of
3-N-cyclohexylamino-acetanilide as a yllow solid. 1H NMR (CDCl3) δ 7.81
(s, 1H), 7.02 (t, J = 6.4 Hz, 1 H), 6.99 (s, 1 H), 6.62 (d, J = 6.4 Hz, 1
H), 6.29 (d, J = 6.4 Hz, 1 H), 3.40 (s, b, 1H), 3.18 (tt, J = 8.0, 3.0
Hz, 1 H), 2.08 (s, 3 H), 1.98 (dd, J = 10.0, 2.0 Hz, 2 H), 1.70 (dt, J =
10.8, 2.8 Hz, 2 H), 1.59 (dt, J = 10.0, 3.0 Hz, 1 H), 1.26-1.34 (m, 2 H),
1.04-1.23 (m, 3 H); 13C NMR (CDCl3) δ 168.64, 147.95, 139.03, 129.43,
108.80, 108.17, 104.75, 51.52, 31.22, 25.78, 24.84, 24.47. Anal. Calcd.
For C14H20N2O: C, 72.38; H, 8.68; N, 12.06. Found: C, 72.24; H, 8.64; N,
11.85.
