$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 2.2.1. Thermolytic Preparation of Ru2(DPhF)3NH(C13H10N2) (3a).
Thermolysis in vacuo of dark violet solid 1a (28.7 mg, 0.0280 mmol) at
160 °C for 48 h yielded a dark violet solid mixture containing 3a in
addition to side products. The solid mixture was extracted with dry
CH2Cl2 (10 mL) and crystallized from CH2Cl2 and hexanes to yield small
X-ray-quality violet crystals of 3a after 7 days at -20 °C. Yield: 20.7
mg, 74.2%. Solid samples of 3a exposed to air were found to be highly
hygroscopic, as indicated by the presence of water in the elemental
analysis. Anal. Calcd for 3a •H2O: C, 61.4; H, 4.53; N, 12.4. Found: C,
61.4; H, 4.40; N, 12.4 (CHN analyzed using V2O5 catalyst). MALDITOF: m/z
= 1001.2 [3a]+. UV-vis: λ (ε) = 525 nm (8900). IR (KBr, cm-1): 3405 b,
3055 m, 3021 w, 1940 w, 1644 m, 1617 s, 1582 s, 1538 m, 1261 w, 1008 w,
808 m, 571 w.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM thermal, alternative preparation shown
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
