$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure: In a dry box, aryl halide
(2.0 mmol), HBPin (512 mg, 4.0 mmol), (Ind)Ir(COD) (16.6 mg, 0.04 mmol, 2
mol%) and dmpe (6.0 mg, 0.04 mmol, 2 mol%) or dppe (15.9 mg, 0.04 mmol, 2
mol%) were transferred into a thick-walled air-free flask equipped with a
magnetic stirring bar. The flask was sealed, removed from the glove box,
and stirred at 150 °C (dmpe) or 100 °C (dppe) until the reaction was
judged complete by GC-FID. The reaction mixture was allowed to cool to
room temperature and subsequently placed under vacuum for 1-2 h. The
thick walled flask was brought into the dry box and anhydrous K3PO4 (594
mg, 2.8 mmol, 1.4 eq), Pd2dba3 (18.3 mg, 0.02 mmol, 1 mol%), P(t-Bu)3
(12.1 mg, 0.06 mmol, 3 mol%) or
2-dicyclohexylphosphino-2’-(N,N-dimethylamino) biphenyl (31.5 mg, 0.08
mmol, 4 mol%) or 2-(dicyclohexylphosphino)biphenyl (28 mg, 0.08 mmol, 4
mol%), amine (2.4-2.6 mmol, 1.2-1.3 eq) and DME (3mL) were added. The
flask was then sealed, removed from the dry box and stirred at 100 °C
until the reaction was judged complete by GC-FID. After completion, the
reaction mixture was extracted three times with ether. The combined
organics were washed with brine followed by water, dried over MgSO4, and
concentrated under reduced pressure. The crude material was then
subjected to column chromatography. Table 2, Entry 11:
N-Phenyl-3-(N,N-dimethyl)-5-(4,4,5,5-tetramethyl-1,3,2-
dioxaboryl)aniline. The general procedure was applied to
3-chloro-N,N-dimethyl aniline (312.0 mg, 2.0 mmol). The borylation step
was carried out neat with HBPin (512.0 mg, 4.0 mmol) and dmpe (6.0 mg,
0.04 mmol, 2 mol%) at 150 °C for 18 h. The amination step was then
carried out using 2-dicyclohexylphosphino-2’-(N,N-dimethylamino) biphenyl
(31.5 mg, 0.08 mmol, 4 mol%) and aniline (242.1 mg, 2.6 mmol) at 100 °C
for 17 h. Column chromatography (pentane/THF 5:1) furnished the desired
product (494.0 mg, 73%) as a white solid, mp 133-134 °C. 1H NMR (C6D6,
300 MHz) δ 7.39 (d, J = 1.5 Hz, 1 H), 7.32 (d, J = 2.5 Hz, 1 H),
7.10-7.04 (m, 2 H), 6.98-6.94 (m, 2 H), 6.79-6.74 (m, 1 H), 6.55 (t, J =
2.3 Hz, 1 H), 5.15 (br s, 1 H), 2.52 (s, 6 H), 1.14 (s, 12 H). 13C NMR
(C6D6, 75 MHz) δ 151.7 (C), 144.6 (C), 143.8 (C), 129.5 (CH), 120.3 (CH),
117.6 (CH), 114.8 (CH), 113.4 (CH), 106.6 (CH), 83.6 (C), 40.3 (CH3),
24.9 (CH3). 11B NMR (C6D6, 96 MHz) δ 32.03. FT-IR (neat): 3366, 3048,
2978, 2932, 2801, 1584, 1497, 1470, 1437, 1414, 1383, 1298, 1275, 1250,
1217, 1143, 1120, 1016, 968, 849, 754, 736, 708, 698 cm-1. LRMS m/z (rel.
int.) 338 (100), 309 (7) 237 (5). Anal. Calcd for C20H27BN2O2: C, 71.02;
H, 8.04; N, 8.28. Found: C, 71.05; H, 8.05; N, 8.25.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective, no solvent in stage 1
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
